mark :12
author Sven Olsen <sven@acme-fin.io> 1741767240 +0100
committer Sven Olsen <sven@acme-fin.io> 1741767240 +0100
data 573
fix(sync): cap batch at 50 after INC-212 (#148)

Acme Ledger enforces 60 requests per minute per API token and answers
429 above it. runNightlySync fans out one POST per entry in a batch, so a
batch of 500 fired 500 requests at once. On 2025-03-11 the nightly sync
was throttled for six hours and the 06:00 close ran on stale balances
(INC-212).

50 entries per batch plus the 1s pause keeps us under the limit with
headroom for the webhook path, which uses the same token. Raising the
batch needs a per-token limit increase from Acme first (ticket ACME-3312,
still open).
